Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 00 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING CLOSE TO THE SUPERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  RADIATION CHANGES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 31                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm portion of unremarkable breast tissue  No discrete lesions are identified  A portion is frozen as frozen section  1  and resubmitted in cassette B  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in cassette A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a total right mastectomy specimen  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm right breast with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm tan unremarkable skin ellipse  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm ill defined  firm to hard gray mass  0 2cm from the superior resection margin adjacent to the skin ellipse and 3 0cm from the deep margin  A portion of the lesion is frozen as frozen section  2 and frozen section  3  and submitted respectively in cassettes C and D  further sectioning of the mass reveals focally hemorrhagic portions  The remaining breast parenchyma is predominantly unremarkable adipose tissue interspersed with a moderate amount of dense white fibrous connective tissue  Also received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of irregular adipose tissue from which two tan pink firm lymph nodes are identified measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  Section Code  E F  mass with closest superior margin  G I  remainder of mass  J L  irregular pink white fibrous areas  M  axillary lymph n