Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Cytology  Cytology Report  ML 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   CASE  ML 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  FNAB Clinic  ACC 270  Resident   Reports To   MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D         FINE NEEDLE ASPIRATION BIOPSY SERVICE   PATIENT EVALUATION    Chief Complaint  This 65 year old woman was referred to the fine needle  aspiration clinic by Dr  Specht for consultation and diagnosis     Clinical History  She has a history of left breast cancer and now presents  with a 4cm right axillary mass and possible supraclavicular lymph node     Physical Examination  Laterality was established according to departmental  protocol  Examination of the right axilla revealed a 4 0cm firm fixed mass   Examination of the right supraclavicular area revealed a subtle firm ridge with  pulsation but no definite lymph node     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and complications were explained to the patient and  consent was obtained   Site  1  1 aspirate was performed of the right axillary lymph node using 23  gauge needles without anesthesia and without complications  Multiple slides  were stained for immediate evaluation  additional tissue was submitted for  further evaluation  See corresponding cytology report MN 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Site  2  1 aspirate was performed of the right supraclavicular lymph node using  23 gauge needles without anesthesia and without complications  Multiple slides  were stained for immediate evaluation  additional tissue was submitted for  further evaluation  See corresponding cytology report MN 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Rapid Interpretation     1  Right axillary lymph node  fine needle aspiration biopsy   Ductal carcinoma     2  Right supraclavicular soft tissue  fine needle aspiration biopsy   Fibroadipose tissue  no lymph node present     Disposi