Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 MAY 95 ACCESSIONED ON  30 MAY 95 at 15 40 CLINICAL DATA  Inflammatory carcinoma of the right breast  status post chemotherapy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA   90    MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  WITH EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION  PROMINENT IN THE DERMIS    INFLAMMATORY CARCINOMA    AND WITH METASTASIS TO 5 OF 5 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  WITH EXTRANODAL EXTENSION  SEE NOTE  2  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  MICROPAPILLARY TYPE WITH NECROSIS  10   NOTE  The tumor measures 7 0cm in greatest diameter and is grossly 2 0cm from the nearest margin  however  microscopic foci of tumor both in breast tissue and in lymphatics are present throughout the breast and are found within 0 3cm of inked margins  Diagnosis by  Jeoffry Brennick  MD Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 06 Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                      ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     Levels  Block  O   reveal one additional lymph node with metastatic adenocarcinoma  and additional tissue processed  submitted as block  Q   reveals two lymph nodes with metastatic adenocarcinoma  a total of eight of eight  8 8  lymph nodes are positive for adenocarcinoma  Added by  Jeoffry Brennick  MD Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 54 Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 07 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast and axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 10 0cm breast with a short stitch designating the superior edge and a long stitch designating the lateral edge  with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The overlying skin  REMOVED_DATE x 17 0cm  has a 1 0cm nipple with a 4 5cm areola  The nipple is focally hyperpigmented and firm  The areola is centrally hypopigmented  peripherally hyperpigmented and diffuse firm  The skin inferior and lateral to the nipple is firm  No definitive scar is identified on the skin  The breast is sectioned to reveal an irregular area of hard  stellate tissue with focal necrosis  located in the inferior breast  and measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMO