Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  MS 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   CASE  MS 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Private Outside MGH    Path Subspecialty Service  Hemepath  Results To  LEONARD LLOYD ELLMAN  M D   GABRIELLE M BAKER  M D   Resident  Gabrielle Baker  M D   Signed Out by  Judith A Ferry  M D              Addended Report                Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Diagnostic Information  CLINICAL DATA   Chronic anemia and massive splenomegaly  lymphoma       FINAL DIAGNOSIS   BONE MARROW  RIGHT ILIAC CREST   BIOPSY  ASPIRATE  CLOT SECTION AND PERIPHERAL  SMEAR   HYPERCELLULAR MARROW WITH INVOLVEMENT BY A LOW GRADE B CELL LYMPHOMA    LEUKEMIA    SEE NOTE      NOTE  The bone marrow biopsy specimen is adequate for evaluation  The bone  marrow clot specimen contains very scant marrow particles  The marrow  cellularity is overall approximately 80   The myeloid to erythroid ratio is  normal  Myeloid maturation is complete  Erythroid maturation is complete   Megakaryocytes appear adequate  Multiple large lymphoid aggregates are present   in both a paratrabecular and non trabecular distribution  The lymphoid cells  are small to medium sized with irregular nuclear contours and variably abundant  pale cytoplasm  The lymphoid cells overall comprise approximately 50 60  of  total marrow cellularity  and occupy 40 50  of the marrow space  Granulomas  are not identified  Both H E and Giemsa stains were examined to evaluate the  biopsy  Reticulin stain shows 1 2  4 fiber staining     The aspirate smear is adequate for evaluation  A 300 cell differential count  reveals  34  myeloid precursors  30  erythroid precursors  27  lymphocytes  2   monocytes  4  eosinophils  1  basophils  1  promyelocytes  0  blasts  and 1   plasma cells  Myeloid maturation is normal  Erythroid maturation is normal  except for late mitoses  Megakaryocytes appear normal   The lymphocytes are predominantly small forms with condensed chromatin  scant  basophilic cytoplasm  and mild nuclear irregularity  The proportion of  lymphocytes is highly variable from one area to another  with some fields being  predominantly composed of lymphocytes  A smear stained for iron shows abundant  iron stores  no ringed sideroblasts are identified     CBC results from REMOVED_DATE are as follows  WBC  REMOVED_DATE  HCT  REMOVED_DATE  PLT  73   Auto differential from REMOVED_DATE  35  polys  61  lymphocytes  3  monocytes  1   eosinophils  and 0  basophils   Review of the peripheral smear reveals mature leukocytes with scattered mature  lymphoid cells with delicate cytoplasmic processes  consistent with villous  lymphocytes     SUMMARY  In a patient with massive splenomegaly  the findings are suspicious  for marrow involvement by splenic marginal zone lymphoma  Immunostains are in  progress to evaluate the specimen further  results will be reported in an  addendum   See also results of flow cytometry  ML 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    which shows a clonal B cell  population  Also see results of cytogenetics  CG 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID         GROSS DESCRIPTION   Received in B  fixative   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE  x 0 2cm brown firm tissue core submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   after decalcification   Also received is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm aggregate of blood coagulum submitted in  toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID        Final Diagnosis by Judith A Ferry M D   Electronically signed on Friday  February 05   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 07 18 03PM  By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final  Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed  or corrected the diagnoses               ADDENDUM NOTE   REASON   Additional Diagnostic Information    Immunohistochemistry reveals that the lymphoid aggregates are positive for   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with scattered admixed  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   T cells   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  highlights dendritic meshworks  within lymphoid aggregates  The lymphoid aggregates stain positively for  bcl 2  and are negative for bcl 6  Lymphoid cells are negative for cyclin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  highlights the vasculature  intravascular lymphoid cells are  inconspicuous  IgD dimly stains some B cells  In situ hybridization for kappa  and lambda immunoglobulin light chains shows a few scattered lambda  plasma  cells and many scattered kappa  plasma cells  consistent with a population of  monotypic kappa  plasma cells in a small polytypic background     The findings are consistent with a low grade B cell lymphoma with plasmacytic  differentiation  While the findings are not completely specific  they are most  consistent with marrow involvement by splenic marginal zone lymphoma     This immunoperoxidase test was developed and its performance characteristics  determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital   It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration   FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not  necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and  precision     Selected markers were evaluated by immunohistochemistry as well as flow  cytometry to assess their expression in the context of the tissue architecture       Addendum  1 by Judith A Ferry M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday  February 09   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 58 33PM  By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final  Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed  or corrected the diagnoses     PART A  Bone Marrow  Right Iliac Crest   Biopsy  PART B  Bone Marrow  Aspirate   Smear  PART C  Peripheral Blood  Smear       report_end  , No.
